## THE DECISIONS OF THIS COMMIT (each Tuesday's default as coordinator; each a Question at the stamp)
- **D1: the slice is navigation only (Q1).** Calls 1 to 3 of A2 and nothing else. Why: it lands on its own (one source project, Graph only), it is what every later Teams journey starts from, and it needs no change in another lane's module. The listing of the channel's folder (A2 call 4, `drives/{d}/items/{i}/children`) is NOT here: the OneDrive module's listing addresses `me/drive` only and its reader is `internal` (MEASURED), and plan B2156 line 119 says "If they need a change in OneDrive, the OneDrive lane makes it" (RELAYED). Alternative: build Teams' own drive-scoped listing now (a second item reader beside OneDrive's; about 0.5 lock-day more, a re-draft).
- **D2: the paging walk is the Graph layer's** (`GraphClient.GetPagesAsync`, `GraphClient.cs:123`: next link on the base origin only, a loop refused, page `maxPages + 1` refused, its summary, MEASURED by reading). The module adds the item rules and its own page bound (a constructor argument, default `GraphOptions.DefaultMaxPages` = 100, `GraphOptions.cs:12`). Cost: a next link is bound to the origin, not to the same call's form (OneDrive's browser binds the form too); a next link of another Graph path on the same host would be followed (named limit R11).
- **D3: the id rules.** Team id: exactly 36 characters and `Guid.TryParseExact(teamId, "D", out _)` (Microsoft's pages show team ids as hyphenated GUIDs, FACTS 6; the length test first, so padded text never reaches the GUID reader: whether that reader trims white space is not relied on). Channel id: 1 to 256 characters of ASCII letters, digits and `: @ . _ -`, not `.` or `..` (Microsoft's "List channels" page shows `19:561fbdbbfca848a484f0a6f00ce9dbbd@thread.tacv2`, FACTS 6; `:` and `@` are allowed in a URI path segment by RFC 3986 section 3.3, general knowledge). Drive and item ids: the OneDrive module's item rule (`^[A-Za-z0-9!._-]+$`, 1 to 256, not `.` or `..`; Microsoft's "Get filesFolder" page shows the drive id `b!2SInBlQ...-hd` and the item id `01H7CFEKENJSSIUHGADZBKODARINQC5JMD`, FACTS 6). Every id in its rule is sent AS WRITTEN; whether Graph answers a channel id with `:` and `@` unescaped as the same channel is UNMEASURED (Microsoft's own `@odata.context` example writes it escaped, `19%3A...%40thread.skype`, FACTS 6). Q2.
- **D4: the files folder is read by its `id`, a `folder` facet that is an object, and `parentReference.driveId`.** Microsoft's page: "returns ... a driveItem object" and its example carries all three (FACTS 6). Its note that a migrated private channel's filesFolder "returns the root folder's driveItem" (FACTS 6) is a named limit (R10): whether a drive root carries the `folder` facet is UNMEASURED.
- **D5: the channel listing asks `$select=id,displayName`** (`ChannelSelect`): the page says "Use `$select` to exclude the **email** property to improve performance" (FACTS 6). `membershipType` is not read in this slice (Q3).
- **D6: nothing is cached** (the source app keeps a navigation cache, A2 line 324, RELAYED): every call asks Graph. Q4.
- **D7: the failure type.** `TeamsBrowseException` with `TeamsFailure` `MalformedItem` (page and item numbers from 1) or `MalformedFolder` (page 0, item 0); message `Teams call failed: <kind>, page <n>, item <n>.` only. A Graph-layer failure leaves as its own `GraphCallException`, unwrapped.
- **D8: new cells only; no landed cell or helper line changes; nothing returns early on any platform. Local CodeQL is NOT runnable on this machine** (FACTS 7).

