## HEAVY (other seats and gates share this machine and the heavy lock)
A heavy job = `dotnet restore`, `dotnet build`, `dotnet test`, `dotnet publish`, a run of a test executable. **Every heavy job goes through `<lane>/gate/heavy.py`, in the foreground, ONE at a time; you never start `dotnet` or a test executable any other way** (`mutants_c3.py run` calls your `heavy.py` for each of its jobs). A job is `python3 -I '<lane>/gate/heavy.py' '<lane>' 'B2199 seat X102' <label> '<clone>' [K=V ...] -- dotnet <arguments>` (or a test executable's absolute path and `-noColor`), a new label for every job; `CI=true` and `TIMEOUT=<s>` go before the --. The runner removes `CI` from the environment unless you give `CI=true` (its line 279, MEASURED): the unlocked restore of Step 3 is the one job WITHOUT `CI=true`. **The runner is the counting runner B2172 (Q8):** with `<project>/.tools/heavy-slots` ABSENT (as at drafting) it reads load1 FIRST and waits while it is 7 or more (at most 30 minutes, then `BLOCKED: load`), THEN takes the lock by `mkdir` of EXACTLY `/Volumes/Datasec_DEV/!CODING/Datasec/OXPd_2/.tools/wave1-heavy.lock.d`, the same folder the canonical runner takes, so it waits behind any canonical-runner seat or gate; with `heavy-slots` = 2 (written only by Tuesday, never by you) a second slot `wave1-heavy.lock.d.2` opens after two load reads 120 s apart, both under 24, and the total of heavy jobs on the machine stays at most 2 (FACTS 8). It writes `owner.txt` (with `slot <k>` and a `cwd` line), runs the ONE command in its own process group under a time bound (900 s by default; on time-out TERM then KILL to the whole group and an `ORPHAN <pid> <cmd>` line for anything left holding the clone), and releases the slot by MOVING the folder to `<lane>/_quarantine/locks/` (its header, MEASURED by `sed -n 1,30p`). Exit 96 `BLOCKED: checkout busy` means another job of YOURS holds a slot in the same clone: never start a second one. **An `owner.txt` is never yours to break. Allow 30 minutes of waits per job and about 90 in all** (this lane has about 39 heavy jobs, DERIVED: Step 1 3, Step 3 4, Step 4 3 + 16 for the eight mutants + 2, Step 5 5, and the moved-main case adds none); `BLOCKED: lock held <its owner line>` after that is a relaunch for Tuesday, not a finding. Never hold the lock while you read, edit or wait on a hosted run. After any rc 124, read `ps -axo pid,ppid,etime,command` for anything left and say so. **Shell form:** ONE simple command per call; no `$( ... )` inside a loop, no long `&&` chains; multi-step logic goes into a `python3 -I` script under `<lane>/scratch/` that you then run. zsh does not split an unquoted variable, and `$NAME:` followed by a letter is a zsh modifier: write each command out in full or wrap it in `bash -c`. A run longer than a tool call's foreground cap (the whole solution, the mutants, `hosted3.py --wait`) runs as ONE background call and you wait for its end.

